# md5 checksums of the dataset files used for every published ATOMTRICK run.
# Paths are relative to the repository root.  Check with:   md5sum -c --ignore-missing scripts/data/checksums.md5
#
# IMPORTANT: processed NPZs you REGENERATE with scripts/data/prepare_*.py will NOT match the
# file-level md5s below even when every array is bit-identical (numpy.savez_compressed stamps each
# zip member with the current time).  Verify regenerated files with the array-level manifest instead:
#     python scripts/data/verify_data.py        (reads scripts/data/checksums_arrays.tsv)
# The file-level md5s are for byte-identical copies of our processed files and for the raw downloads.
#
# --- Raw downloads (scripts/data/download_*.sh) ---
